WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.502
To define area rigorously, trap it between quantities already understood

00:00:04.502 --> 00:00:06.963
Divide the interval into equal pieces

00:00:06.963 --> 00:00:15.167
For an increasing function, the left endpoint gives a lower rectangle height and the right endpoint gives an upper height.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:19.990
With four pieces, each rectangle has width one quarter

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:25.078
The four lower heights are zero, one quarter, one half, and three quarters

00:00:25.078 --> 00:00:30.167
Their sum times the shared width gives three eighths as the lower estimate.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:37.016
For n equal pieces, summing the endpoint heights gives these upper and lower expressions

00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:39.395
Their difference is one over n

00:00:39.395 --> 00:00:46.133
As the partition gets finer, the entire uncertainty shrinks to zero, trapping the integral at one half.

00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:52.904
The finite pictures motivate the argument; the shrinking bound proves the result

00:00:52.904 --> 00:01:01.109
More generally, a bounded function is Riemann integrable when partitions can make upper and lower sums arbitrarily close

00:01:01.109 --> 00:01:04.300
Not every bounded function meets that condition.
